What is an Endpoint in Amazon SageMaker? 🚀

An Endpoint is a live URL/API connection where you send new data to your trained machine learning model and receive a prediction.

====

Simple flow
User / Application
       │
       │ Sends new input
       ▼
SageMaker Endpoint
       │
       ▼
inference.py
       │
       ▼
Trained Model
(model.tar.gz)
       │
       ▼
Prediction Result
       │
       ▼
User / Application

=====
In your project


You trained an Insurance Prediction Model.

After deployment:

New Customer Details
Age, BMI, Children, Smoker, etc.
            │
            ▼
     SageMaker Endpoint
            │
            ▼
     Insurance Prediction Model
            │
            ▼
 Predicted Insurance Cost 💰

===

Simple example

Your application sends:

{
  "age": 35,
  "bmi": 28.5,
  "children": 2,
  "smoker": 0
}

The SageMaker Endpoint sends this data to your deployed model.

Then the model returns something like:

Predicted Insurance Cost: ₹45,000

